idf-component-manager 3.1.2 prepare.py:140 用 bool(args.use_sdk_json)，ESP-IDF 首遍传的
"FALSE" 为真，于是按上一个板型的 sdkconfig.json 求值 $CONFIG 规则，同一 build 目录换板时
cn_dial 被错删/错拉。源文件作废时让派生文件同步作废，管理器回到缺键 exit 10、用新配置重试的路径。

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/build.py | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/build.py b/scripts/build.py
index 3b2e56e..f441c3c 100755
--- a/scripts/build.py
+++ b/scripts/build.py
@@ -1439,6 +1439,17 @@ def _configure_build(
             sdkconfig_old.unlink()
         sdkconfig.replace(sdkconfig_old)
 
+    # build/config/sdkconfig.json is derived from the sdkconfig we just retired, so retire it
+    # too. The component manager evaluates `$CONFIG{...}` rules in idf_component.yml (e.g.
+    # cn_dial's RH_DIAL_DEPS) against this file. ESP-IDF intends to skip it on the first pass
+    # (tools/cmake/build.cmake passes --use_sdk_json=FALSE), then regenerate Kconfig and retry.
+    # But idf-component-manager 3.1.2 checks bool(args.use_sdk_json) in
+    # prepare_components/prepare.py:140, and bool("FALSE") is True. So it reads the previous
+    # board's values, and switching boards in one build dir dropped or pulled cn_dial wrongly
+    # (logs/build-sleepfix-spotpear.log:104-114). With the stale file gone, a missing key
+    # makes the manager exit 10, and ESP-IDF retries with the freshly generated file.
+    Path("build/config/sdkconfig.json").unlink(missing_ok=True)
+
     fragment = Path("build/xiaozhi-build.sdkconfig.defaults")
     fragment.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
     fragment.write_text(
